  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "During its November 2026 Board of Governors Meeting, Bank Indonesia announced a 25-basis-point increase to the benchmark BI-Rate, bringing it to 6 percent. This monetary policy adjustment is aimed at strengthening the domestic currency and managing economic stability. In parallel with this decision, the central bank revealed plans to expand its financial infrastructure by involving state-owned banks, known as Himbara, in renminbi clearing processes beginning in 2027. Market analysts and banking representatives are now assessing how these adjustments might influence banking liquidity and future credit growth, following reports that bank credit had expanded by 13.21 percent in October 2026. The government is also monitoring the broader economic environment to ensure stability as financial institutions navigate the implications of the new interest rate level on consumer loans and business financing.",
